  document.getElementById('geo-policy-version').insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin','<p><strong>NWS alert rules:</strong> Only Actual Alert / Update messages with a valid time, an area polygon and a source fetched in the last 5 minutes count toward the current level. CAP Severity maps Minor → INFO, Moderate → WATCH, Severe → HIGH, Extreme → CRITICAL; Urgency must be Immediate / Expected. Certainty Possible / Unlikely caps the level at WATCH; Observed / Likely keeps the mapped level. Cancelled, expired, future, incomplete or stale alerts never set a current level.</p><p><strong>Spatial matching:</strong> A point inside a polygon, an accuracy circle fully inside an area, and a possible overlap near the edge are reported separately; edges use a 25 m prototype buffer. The highest valid match wins, but an unconfirmed address gives only a conditional match; a conflicting or outdated confirmation returns the summary to unknown. A valid operator circle adds separately labeled context and is never an official area. Synthetic demo areas never set a current level.</p>');
